    },
    {
      "id": "claim_662ea9b9ec004cd98a9410f3d8b63ddd",
      "statement": "Offer establishment creates the RTCPeerConnection with a data channel (ordered:false), generates the local offer, then waits for ICE candidates to finish — or a 3-second timeout (WAIT_ICE_CANDIDATES_TIMEOUT) — before building the offer link from the encoded SDP.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L62-L134",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a63b7a78e4adac8bcd20d2fce09e289aefda03b4efbb420058c91a9a8f9fdce7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_168fa874ca494eb0b49c143450d46e27",
      "statement": "The answer peer decodes the attacker-controllable `s` URL param via sdpDecode (which throws synchronously on empty, invalid-base64, or non-SDP input) inside a try/catch that surfaces an 'Invalid SDP in link' error toast instead of crashing the page during load (PR #45), awaits the validated p-param key import, creates a local answer, and produces an answer code of the form sdpEncode(answerSdp) + '|' + base64(RSA public key), with the same 3-second ICE candidate timeout fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/ReceivePage.svelte#L116-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23e4ffa4615576a8bdf315aa3fd11d35228c8372c48b0b2215152c78117c9082:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c2c408a79a5f495fa0bf3c5b1efcccdb",
      "statement": "All data-channel traffic is proto3-framed Message bytes: a file id plus exactly one of metaData (name, size, type, encrypted AES key), chunk (file body slice), or receiveEvent (receiver control event); there is no ad-hoc text protocol on the channel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/proto/message.proto#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f8c0ab1d2ddf1af4c03d3743789407e5f7307442c33e3dfe52c728531974356:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_311d6dea83ac47ecbb8e7a3de45ee72a",
      "statement": "Both pages dispatch incoming data-channel messages with the same oneof switch: metaData routes to Receiver.onMetaData, chunk to Receiver.onChunkData, and receiveEvent to Sender.onReceiveEvent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L86-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9c7eb1f69cb9764cf555f5de72fd7552402aeb3dd63f9c401f50a9f98524e2a:"
        },
        {
